1
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:02,660
Wealth, fame, power.

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:04,597
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:07,177
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,260 --> 00:00:10,436
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,975
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,420
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:16,620
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:19,060
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:24,217
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:26,737
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,820 --> 00:00:29,517
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:34,980
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:40,440
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:42,700
One piece.

15
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:52,577
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:58,477
Your heart will be your guide,
raise the sails and take the helm.

17
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:01,137
That legendary place.

18
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:03,817
That the end of the map reveals.

19
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:06,657
Is only legendary.

20
00:01:06,740 --> 00:01:10,117
Till someone proves it real.

21
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:12,557
Through it all.

22
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:14,477
Through all the trouble and times.

23
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:16,817
Through the heartache
and through the pain.

24
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:21,180
Know that I will be there to stand by you.

25
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:24,160
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

26
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:30,540
So come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

27
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:36,020
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

28
00:01:37,220 --> 00:01:42,440
There's always room for you
if you want to be my friend.

29
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:46,880
We are, we are on a cruise.

30
00:01:48,420 --> 00:01:49,700
We are.

31
00:01:51,860 --> 00:01:53,777
Don't call it murder, Django.

32
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:55,960
I don't like the sound of it.

33
00:01:56,180 --> 00:01:57,860
Oh, right. Accident.

34
00:01:58,100 --> 00:02:00,200
It's an accident that you planned.

35
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:04,020
Uh, what are those guys talking about?

36
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:05,520
Just be quiet.

37
00:02:05,820 --> 00:02:08,317
Maybe if we listen a little
closer, we can find out.

38
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:10,100
We can't simply kill her.

39
00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:14,957
It is critical to our plan that Miss
Kaya perishes in an unfortunate accident.

40
00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:16,620
So don't screw that up.

41
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:19,480
So basically, on your signal,

42
00:02:19,620 --> 00:02:21,257
the men and I stormed
the village and manage

43
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:23,811
to accidentally kill the little rich girl.

44
00:02:24,460 --> 00:02:27,537
Then you get her inheritance
and we all get paid, right?

45
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:28,500
You moron!

46
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:30,337
Your ignorance is astounding.

47
00:02:30,420 --> 00:02:33,817
We're not related, so how could
I inherit anything from her?

48
00:02:33,900 --> 00:02:35,460
You'll work very hard to.

49
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:37,860
No, Django, I won't.

50
00:02:38,220 --> 00:02:39,300
Now listen to me.

51
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:41,277
This is the most important part.

52
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:45,637
Before you kill her, you'll use your
hypnosis to make Kaya write her will.

53
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:50,080
And it will say I leave my entire
fortune to my butler, Klahadore.

54
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:57,060
Then and only then will I have undisputed
control of her enormous fortune,

55
00:02:57,400 --> 00:02:59,820
and no one will suspect a thing.

56
00:03:01,340 --> 00:03:05,857
I have spent three long years gaining
the trust of everyone around me so that

57
00:03:05,940 --> 00:03:10,646
it would be unsurprising for her to leave
the entirety of her inheritance to me.

58
00:03:11,140 --> 00:03:13,800
Three years as a butler for this, huh?

59
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:18,400
You sure had us scared
back then, Captain Kuro.

60
00:03:19,180 --> 00:03:23,356
Three years ago, you suddenly said
you were giving up life as a pirate.

61
00:03:23,740 --> 00:03:26,857
In no time at all, you set
up someone to be your double.

62
00:03:26,940 --> 00:03:30,460
Then you let the world see
Captain Kuro get executed.

63
00:03:41,340 --> 00:03:45,077
Only now do I understand that was
just the beginning of this plan.

64
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:47,278
You are the man of a thousand plans.

65
00:03:47,780 --> 00:03:49,437
Never call me that again.

66
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,660
I abandoned that name years ago.

67
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:56,337
I now wish to obtain my wealth without
attracting the attention of the government.

68
00:03:56,420 --> 00:03:58,460
In other words, I'm a pacifist.

69
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:02,200
The pacifist you are.

70
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:07,280
Murdering an entire family doesn't
exactly qualify as peaceful.

71
00:04:08,860 --> 00:04:09,690
Hold on.

72
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:11,757
I haven't murdered an entire family.

73
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:13,537
The father's death wasn't planned.

74
00:04:13,620 --> 00:04:15,777
Whatever you say, it
makes no difference to me.

75
00:04:15,860 --> 00:04:19,154
If it's all the same to you,
hurry up and give the word.

76
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:20,829
The crew is getting bored.

77
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:24,277
We've been wading in the waters
near here for over a week.

78
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:27,360
And the men are growing
more anxious by the minute.

79
00:04:33,320 --> 00:04:34,480
This is horrible.

80
00:04:35,060 --> 00:04:36,760
This is really horrible.

81
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:41,487
What are they talking about?

82
00:04:41,640 --> 00:04:43,500
Is it bad guy stuff? What?

83
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:45,097
Weren't you listening to any of that?

84
00:04:45,180 --> 00:04:47,592
Those guys aren't just bad, they're evil.

85
00:04:48,320 --> 00:04:51,877
Captain Kuro is known to be the most
devious, skimming pirate around.

86
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:55,957
And though he's known for his smarts,
he's legendary for his brutality.

87
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:59,737
Word had it that the Marines caught
and executed him three years ago.

88
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:04,160
But Captain Kuro is alive and
well, posing as Clawdor the butler.

89
00:05:04,380 --> 00:05:09,204
And he's had his diabolical sights set on
Kaya's fortune for the last three years.

90
00:05:12,100 --> 00:05:14,100
First, they'll attack the village.

91
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:16,020
They'll kill Kaya!

92
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:20,440
This is bad!

93
00:05:20,700 --> 00:05:22,460
This is seriously bad!

94
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:27,840
Hey, get down! They'll see you!

95
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:29,360
Hey, bad guys!

96
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:31,618
You better stay away from that girl!

97
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:33,740
Who are you?

98
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:35,230
You idiot!

99
00:05:35,313 --> 00:05:36,143
They've spotted you!

100
00:05:36,226 --> 00:05:39,337
Come on, hurry up and hide before they
decide you need a long, slow death!

101
00:05:39,420 --> 00:05:43,420
Well, now, if it isn't Usopp,
the mischievous town liar...

102
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:45,590
Oh, no!

103
00:05:45,760 --> 00:05:46,760
I'm spotted, too!

104
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:49,620
Did you hear anything?

105
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:52,180
Uh, no, nothing at all.

106
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:53,110
I don't know what you mean.

107
00:05:53,193 --> 00:05:54,023
We didn't hear a peep.

108
00:05:54,106 --> 00:05:54,936
We just got here.

109
00:05:55,019 --> 00:05:56,317
So, we didn't hear
anything about anything.

110
00:05:56,400 --> 00:05:57,257
We heard it all.

111
00:05:57,340 --> 00:05:58,170
Shut up!

112
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:05,540
Well, if you say so.

113
00:06:08,300 --> 00:06:12,260
Pay attention, boys, and
watch this ring closely.

114
00:06:13,180 --> 00:06:14,010
Okay.

115
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:15,217
Don't you get it?

116
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:16,357
It's some kind of weapon.

117
00:06:16,440 --> 00:06:17,297
We've got to run.

118
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:20,860
By the count of Jango, you
will be in a deep sleep.

119
00:06:21,280 --> 00:06:22,280
Are you ready?

120
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:24,397
One, run for cover.

121
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:25,857
Two, he's going to kill us.

122
00:06:25,940 --> 00:06:26,770
Jango!

123
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:33,277
Jango, you idiot.

124
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:36,007
I see you're still
falling asleep on the job.

125
00:06:37,860 --> 00:06:39,160
Hey, be careful.

126
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:40,635
You're going to fall.

127
00:06:44,960 --> 00:06:47,607
He had to go and fall
off a cliff, didn't he?

128
00:06:48,060 --> 00:06:48,942
A pity, really.

129
00:06:49,060 --> 00:06:50,217
I didn't mean to kill him.

130
00:06:50,300 --> 00:06:52,771
But there's no way he could have survived.

131
00:06:52,880 --> 00:06:54,400
This can't be happening.

132
00:06:55,340 --> 00:06:56,600
They killed him.

133
00:06:57,060 --> 00:06:58,720
He's really dead.

134
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:01,191
What about the other one?

135
00:07:01,400 --> 00:07:02,871
Shall I take care of him?

136
00:07:03,360 --> 00:07:04,301
There's no need.

137
00:07:04,660 --> 00:07:07,580
Everything he could say
would sound like lies.

138
00:07:09,020 --> 00:07:12,597
Jango, tomorrow at daybreak, the
men are to attack the village.

139
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:16,297
Rough up the villagers some and tear up
their homes a little for good measure.

140
00:07:16,380 --> 00:07:20,500
And above all, make sure Miss
Kaya's death looks accidental.

141
00:07:22,080 --> 00:07:22,910
Tomorrow?

142
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:25,140
Just accept it, Usopp.

143
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:30,402
There is nothing you can say or do to warn
the villagers of this impending tragedy.

144
00:07:35,360 --> 00:07:37,160
Are you sure about that one?

145
00:07:37,340 --> 00:07:38,360
Of course I am.

146
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:39,900
My plans are flawless.

147
00:07:45,180 --> 00:07:46,660
I can't believe this.

148
00:07:46,820 --> 00:07:47,820
This is terrible.

149
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:49,511
I've got to do something.

150
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:52,897
Everyone in the village I
grew up with is in danger.

151
00:07:52,980 --> 00:07:54,745
And Kaia's going to be killed.

152
00:07:57,300 --> 00:07:58,300
Who are you?

153
00:07:58,720 --> 00:08:01,280
I'm Usopp, brave warrior of the sea.

154
00:08:03,220 --> 00:08:05,077
I heard you've been a little down lately,

155
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:06,977
so I thought I'd tell you
a story to cheer you up.

156
00:08:07,060 --> 00:08:09,497
You would do well to
mind your own business.

157
00:08:09,580 --> 00:08:12,992
Please leave or I'll call
someone who will make you leave!

158
00:08:16,100 --> 00:08:16,930
And then?

159
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:18,497
What happened after that?

160
00:08:18,580 --> 00:08:19,698
I fought, of course

161
00:08:21,820 --> 00:08:22,650
No!

162
00:08:31,460 --> 00:08:33,240
Captain! Hold on.

163
00:08:33,440 --> 00:08:36,028
I thought Luffy was
supposed to be with him.

164
00:08:38,040 --> 00:08:38,870
Captain!

165
00:08:40,260 --> 00:08:41,560
Hey, where's Luffy?

166
00:08:41,660 --> 00:08:43,131
Is he still at the shore?

167
00:08:46,760 --> 00:08:49,660
Wow, he looked really upset. But why?

168
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:51,232
Still mad at the butler?

169
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:53,300
Who knows?

170
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:56,520
No, that wasn't just a mad face.

171
00:08:56,900 --> 00:08:58,312
That look was different.

172
00:08:58,480 --> 00:09:00,951
It was a tragic face of sheer desperation.

173
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:04,777
Hey, why don't you guys show us
the way to get down to that shore?

174
00:09:04,860 --> 00:09:06,978
This smells like an adventure to me.

175
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:09,277
Yeah, something happened at the shore.

176
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:11,617
I think this calls for the use of pirates.

177
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:12,582
Enough already.

178
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:14,367
How do we get to this place?

179
00:09:15,860 --> 00:09:16,740
Terrible news.

180
00:09:19,780 --> 00:09:20,610
Pirates!

181
00:09:20,693 --> 00:09:21,523
Pirates are coming!

182
00:09:21,780 --> 00:09:22,620
Everybody run!

183
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:24,940
We don't set a chance!

184
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:26,780
Everybody run! Run!

185
00:09:30,060 --> 00:09:32,257
Tomorrow morning they're
going to attack the village.

186
00:09:32,340 --> 00:09:33,677
We've got to get out of here.

187
00:09:33,760 --> 00:09:34,817
What are you doing?

188
00:09:34,900 --> 00:09:35,730
Run!

189
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:54,700
All right, Usopp.

190
00:09:54,920 --> 00:09:55,757
Enough is enough.

191
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:57,340
We can't take it anymore.

192
00:09:57,560 --> 00:09:59,237
We're putting a stop to this here and now.

193
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:00,177
It's for your own good.

194
00:10:00,260 --> 00:10:01,820
No, it's not like that.

195
00:10:01,980 --> 00:10:04,980
It's the truth this
time, I promise. Stop it.

196
00:10:05,160 --> 00:10:07,197
We all know that you're
nothing but a liar.

197
00:10:07,280 --> 00:10:11,927
It would do you some good to follow
Clawdor's example of hard work and honesty.

198
00:10:12,740 --> 00:10:15,540
Everything he could say
would sound like lies.

199
00:10:18,760 --> 00:10:19,590
Oh, no.

200
00:10:19,880 --> 00:10:22,257
This is exactly what
Clawdor is counting on.

201
00:10:22,340 --> 00:10:25,516
He ignored me because he
knew no one would believe me.

202
00:10:31,520 --> 00:10:33,344
Are these to your liking, miss?

203
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:37,332
Custom made to your exact specifications.

204
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:40,117
It was quite a trip to get them!

205
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:41,920
They're just perfect.

206
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:47,060
Thank you so much for traveling
so far to get them for me?

207
00:10:53,780 --> 00:10:55,217
They're a gift, aren't they?

208
00:10:55,300 --> 00:10:56,860
Yes. As of tomorrow,

209
00:10:57,060 --> 00:11:00,657
it will be exactly three years to
the day since Klahadore arrived here.

210
00:11:00,740 --> 00:11:03,260
He's always taken such good care of me.

211
00:11:03,620 --> 00:11:06,357
He'll be delighted to
receive such a lovely gift.

212
00:11:06,440 --> 00:11:07,380
I hope so.

213
00:11:09,920 --> 00:11:11,277
Please hear me out, everyone!

214
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:13,320
Our lives depend on it! Listen!

215
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:15,617
Pirates are going to attack
the village in the morning!

216
00:11:15,700 --> 00:11:17,957
If we believed every
story you ever told us,

217
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:20,997
we would have run screaming from the
village hundreds of times already.

218
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:21,910
Please believe me!

219
00:11:21,993 --> 00:11:23,078
We don't have time!

220
00:11:23,700 --> 00:11:26,300
I'm not lying this time. I swear.

221
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:27,860
Don't you get it?

222
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,400
They'll murder you all.

223
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:31,835
You'll be lucky if we don't murder you

224
00:11:37,420 --> 00:11:39,185
Get him, don't let him escape.

225
00:11:47,800 --> 00:11:53,137
After three long years of absence, I
made the call for my men and you came.

226
00:11:53,220 --> 00:11:56,817
Your loyalty will be richly rewarded.

227
00:11:56,900 --> 00:12:02,557
I intend on being more than generous
when I divide the take at dawn tomorrow.

228
00:12:02,640 --> 00:12:05,228
Destroy the village to
your heart's content.

229
00:12:13,720 --> 00:12:14,550
What?

230
00:12:14,633 --> 00:12:16,357
Pirates are going to attack the village?

231
00:12:16,440 --> 00:12:18,322
Then they're going to kill Kaya?

232
00:12:19,380 --> 00:12:21,440
Yep, that's what they said.

233
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:22,875
No question about it.

234
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:29,776
So, what made you think it'd
be a good time for a nap?

235
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:31,180
That's the thing.

236
00:12:31,300 --> 00:12:34,829
I don't remember going to sleep
or getting down here at all.

237
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:37,277
This proves that Klahadore is a bad guy.

238
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:38,957
Usopp saw right through him.

239
00:12:39,040 --> 00:12:41,097
I bet he's on his way
to warn the villagers.

240
00:12:41,180 --> 00:12:42,737
So they'll have time to run away.

241
00:12:42,820 --> 00:12:43,977
Well, that's perfect.

242
00:12:44,060 --> 00:12:45,997
Those stupid pirates won't hurt anyone.

243
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:48,477
Because the town will be abandoned
by the time they get there.

244
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:49,757
Yeah, that's right.

245
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:51,917
We'd better run away
too if we want to live.

246
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:54,817
Alright, let's pack our
treasure and run like the wind.

247
00:12:54,900 --> 00:12:59,820
Oh no? What's up?

248
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:03,480
We need to stock up before
the meat shop guy leaves

249
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:07,101
Come on, that's not really
the issue at hand here.

250
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:25,150
Usopp.

251
00:13:31,540 --> 00:13:35,000
Oh god, i was worried
you wouldn't come back.

252
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:39,520
Quick, run kaya, they're gonna kill you!

253
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:41,670
Huh?

254
00:13:41,753 --> 00:13:42,797
Someone's going to kill me?

255
00:13:42,880 --> 00:13:47,115
He's tricked the entire village,
Clador's really a deadly pirate captain

256
00:13:48,440 --> 00:13:49,937
Is this a story?

257
00:13:50,020 --> 00:13:51,820
Well I don't like this one

258
00:13:53,740 --> 00:13:55,877
This isn't one of my
stories, it's the truth.

259
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:57,607
I heard it with my own ears.

